the five smallest TO-1 misses 1535, 2047, 2207, 2287, 2303 ARE in the FROM-1 set (E-lane: their binding constraint is the
   forward Collatz peak).  So the lane's 'unguarded closure' illustrates Q1 in the E-graph lane's sense (every n reaches 1 in E),
   NOT Q2 (1 reaches every m in E).  Direction error in the lane note's finite illustration: REFUTED as labelled, numbers correct.
no E-arrow enters 3Z from outside (3n+1 != 0 mod 3; n/2 = 0 mod 3 only if n = 0 mod 3), while 3 -> 10 leaves 3Z;
